# Identity and Value Objects

- Entity identifiers are generated by the domain — not by the database
- Value Objects encapsulate validation and formatting — an invalid tax ID never exists as an object
- Human-readable business identifiers (e.g., `SSO-2024-00001`) coexist with internal UUIDs
- Sensitive data (tax IDs, email, phone) is masked in logs and API responses

## Value Object Rules

- Immutable after creation
- Equality by value, not reference
- No setters — create a new instance for change
- Validation failures throw domain exceptions at construction
